<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we demonstrate the effectiveness of our proposed model. First, we describe our datasets and its composition. Next, we highlight our training specifications, including the parameters and experimental setup. We then compare the performance of the proposed model with that of other several state-of-the-art models. Lastly, we conduct an ablation study to further analyze the influence and contribution of various components of our model.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dataset</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct our experiments on five benchmark datasets: CIFAR-10 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, CIFAR-100, MNIST <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, SVHN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> and Tiny Imagenet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite> (see Table  <a href="#S4.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ IV-A Dataset ‣ IV Experiments ‣ CoSwin: Convolution Enhanced Hierarchical Shifted Window Attention ForSmall-Scale Vision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>), for the image classification task.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span> overview of datasets.</figcaption>
